# The upstream harness version this tree was taken from. One ISO date on the
# first non-comment line, bumped by every round that changes the harness.
#
# It exists because a vendored copy cannot be dated from the outside: it carries
# the consuming project's git history, not this repository's. Two field reports
# in a row arrived reporting defects that had been fixed upstream for weeks, and
# neither could say which harness it had measured - so every finding had to be
# re-verified by hand before it could be called already-fixed.
#
#   bash scripts/doctor.sh          prints it, so it lands in every environment
#                                   record and every story that quotes one
#   scripts/check-boundaries.sh     refuses an upstream harness change that does
#                                   not bump it
#
# A field report against this harness states the version it measured. An
# unstamped copy predates stamping, which makes it older than every version
# listed here.
2026-09-11
